# Build-time configuration for the React dashboard.
#
# These are consumed by Vite (import.meta.env.VITE_*) and inlined into the
# built JS bundle at BUILD time, not read at container runtime. Only
# variables prefixed VITE_ are exposed to client code; do not rename these.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: leave these unset. QuickLinks.tsx falls back to
# deriving gateway/Prometheus/Grafana URLs from the browser's own
# hostname on the well-known local ports (8081, 9090, 3000), which is
# exactly how the existing local Docker Compose stack works today.
#
# PUBLIC DEPLOYMENT (e.g. Render): set these to the real public URLs of
# the deployed gateway and Prometheus services. Do not commit real URLs
# to this file -- copy it to frontend/.env.production.local (gitignored)
# or set the variables in your hosting provider's build configuration.

# Public HTTPS URL of the deployed API Gateway (no trailing slash).
# Example: https://api-gateway-xxxx.onrender.com
VITE_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_URL=

# Public HTTPS URL of the deployed Prometheus instance (no trailing slash).
# Example: https://api-gateway-prometheus-xxxx.onrender.com
VITE_PROMETHEUS_PUBLIC_URL=

# Grafana is intentionally NOT part of the public deployment (see README
# "Public Deployment" section) and is only available via local
# `docker compose up`. Leave this unset; the Quick Links panel will show
# Grafana as clearly labeled "local only" instead of a broken link.
# Only set this if Grafana is ever deployed publicly in the future.
VITE_GRAFANA_PUBLIC_URL=
